    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Debug\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter should take paint when it's standing on a paint bucket, and paint the square when it isn't. This program has the two branches mixed up. Find the bug and fix it so the Painter does the right thing in each situation.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the code and read what the console says.\r\n2. Look at where the Painter ended up. Is it on a bucket? Does it have any paint?\r\n3. Trace the code. Which branch ran? Is that the right thing for the Painter to do on a bucket?\r\n4. Fix the bug. There is more than one way to fix it.\r\n5. Run again to check your fix, then use Validate.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: this line moves the Painter onto the bucket\nmove()\n\n# Your code goes below\nif is_on_bucket():\n    paint(\"white\")\nelse:\n    take_paint()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
